plan_mode: approved
plan_resume_context: "Continue from Home Assistant Core 2026.8.0 contracts: manifest/list, manifest/get, integration/setup_info, integration/descriptions, integration/wait, entity/source, slugify. Keep private instance evidence redacted."
plan_validation[2]{text,command,expected}:
  Built live E2E completed successfully on Core 2026.7.4; all stable pre-2026.8 handlers passed and slugify was accepted only as a classified unknown_command compatibility boundary.,"HASSIO_READONLY=true bun run test:e2e:live","Setup wizard, six formatters, typed commands, read-only controls, schema, capabilities, and compatibility classification pass without retaining private payloads."
  Authoritative post-refactor release verification is green with exact coverage and privacy-safe live evidence.,"bun run release:verify","All ten release phases pass, 1,343 tests pass, and all four coverage dimensions are exactly 100%."
plan_decisions[1]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-08-05T20:34:34.587Z",codex-root,Use one typed integrations group plus entity-sources and slugify commands; retain ws call for dynamic integration-defined contracts.,These stable Core discovery handlers form a cohesive read-only agent-intelligence surface without pretending all integration commands are static.,Home Assistant Core 2026.8.0 websocket_api/commands.py and live generic-call probes.
plan_discoveries[1]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T20:34:35.312Z",codex-root,"Official public WebSocket documentation covers target discovery while Core 2026.8.0 additionally registers manifest metadata, setup timing, readiness, descriptions, entity sources, and slugify handlers."
